  "conclusion": "No independently reviewed background-plant labels exist, so incidental recall and precision are not measurable and this file cannot say whether whole-frame or tile screening finds more useful weeds. The source subject and lookalike measures concern photos whose subject is the plant; they are sanity checks of each arm, not background-plant evidence. Arm overlap shows how much the choice changes what a reviewer would see.",
  "meaning": "Three readouts of the same window embeddings, each ranking photos by best target margin. At each budget K a reviewer sees the top K photos. 'found' counts labelled-present (photo, species) pairs reached with that species as the suggestion; 'known_false_alarms' counts suggestions on labelled-absent pairs; precision is over labelled items only, so unlabelled photos are counted apart, not as false alarms. None means not measurable (no labels), not zero. Independent labels are reference-collection examples eligible for evaluation and agreeing blind audits, both only on the rank-independent blind audit sample, measured on the incidental review queue and counted only on incidental photos; a species labelled both present and absent is left out as unresolved. Source subject labels are reference photos whose subject is the weed, measured on a pooled queue with lookalike photos; they describe the subject, not background plants, and a lookalike is not a verified absence.",
